    "summary": "High‑energy ’70 set with scorching Speedway jam & fiery Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The show rides a relentless groove, highlighted by the New Speedway Boogie → Nobody's Fault jam and a blistering Turn On Your Lovelight that even captures Pigpen’s shout. Tight transitions like China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider keep the momentum rolling.",
    "review": "On May 14 1970 at Merramac Community College the Dead were in top‑form, delivering an electric set that feels like a snapshot of early‑’70 fire. Jerry’s guitar is “punchy” and “on fire,” especially during the New Speedway Boogie sandwich into the Nobody's Fault jam and the climactic Lovelight where Pigpen’s infamous “Rock the Pig” shout pierces the mix. Bob Weir’s rhythm work shines in the acoustic opener and his classic banter adds humor, though a few reviewers note occasional tuning hiccups on China Cat Sunflower and High Time. The band rides a fast tempo throughout – Friend Of The Devil opens with gusto, the China Cat → Rider segue is tight, and the relentless New Speedway Boogie anchors the set before a soaring Saint Stephen and a rollicking Not Fade Away that lead into an unforgettable Lovelight finale. While most recordings are solid soundboard captures, the Cotsman SBD (gd70‑05‑14.sbd.cotsman.12439.sbeok.shnf) offers the clearest balance with only minor tape hiss, making it the go‑to version for fans wanting to hear every high‑octane moment.",
